      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we start by calculating the number of unique matchups between the teams. Since there are 9 teams, we need to find the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9, which represents the total number of unique matchups. This can be calculated using the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of teams, \\( k \\) is the number of teams to choose, and \\( ! \\) denotes factorial.\n\nHere, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{72}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\nThis means there are 36 unique matchups between the teams. Since each matchup involves 2 games (one played by each team in the matchup), the total number of games played is:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 2 = 72\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the season is \\(\\boxed{72}\\).",
