      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of teams and the number of games played between any two teams.\n2. Calculate the total number of games played in the league by considering all possible pairs of teams and the number of games each pair plays.\n\nThere are 9 teams in the league, and each team plays exactly 3 games with each of the other teams. This means that for each pair of teams, there are 3 games. \n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of unique pairs of teams. The number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{9}{2} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairs of teams. Since each pair plays 3 games, the total number of games played is:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the league is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
